[00:06.13]I remember the feeling,
[00:08.28]warm but uneasy,
[00:10.42]new home, new city,
[00:12.98]low self-esteem.
[03:05.94]I took pill after pill
[03:08.22]just to quiet my head,
[03:10.58]then smoked by the window
[03:13.13]and stayed in my bed.
[03:15.01]Dropped acid alone while
[03:17.55]the ceiling turned strange
[03:19.81]and waited for something
[03:22.04]inside me to change.
[03:23.99]My dealer knew
[03:24.38]when I needed a spark,
[03:25.04]and I called that friendship
[03:25.69]because it was enough.
[03:26.22]At sixteen, I thought
[03:27.12]I had years left to lose.
[03:29.96]At seventeen,
[03:30.34]I had habits to choose.
[03:33.69]I don't miss the fear
[03:35.99]or the things I went through.
[03:38.15]I miss being young enough
[03:40.33]not to know what they'd do.
[03:42.33]My first love came
[03:42.41]through that apartment door.
[03:42.48]I had never let anyone
[03:42.58]that close before.
[03:42.63]I kept the opioids
[03:44.01]hidden where nobody would see,
[03:46.23]took more than I intended
[03:48.84]and kept it all with me.
[03:50.60]I overdosed in silence
[03:53.14]with the bedroom door shut tight,
[03:55.60]then woke up hours later
[03:57.56]and said that I was alright.
[04:00.08]I didn't know what was wrong
[04:02.26]or why I hated my skin.
[04:04.48]I only knew the pills could cut
[04:06.50]the pressure down within.
[04:51.46]I don't call it good,
[04:53.28]and I don't call it bad.
[04:55.36]It held some of the worst
[04:57.52]and the best that I had.
[04:59.63]Now when I remember,
[05:02.15]I can't make it clean.
[05:03.95]I hated those years,
[05:05.95]but I still miss sixteen.
[05:08.72]Newark is traffic
[05:10.41]I pass on the way,
[05:12.53]but part of me stays
[05:14.52]in that bedroom some days.
[05:16.96]I wasn't chasing
[05:27.82]a story to tell.
[05:30.42]I don't miss that bedroom,
[06:28.30]at least not completely,
[06:30.09]but sometimes I miss
[06:31.17]what it meant to be sixteen.
[06:34.11]I remember the feeling,
[06:38.46]warm but uneasy,
[06:39.30]a new home, a new city,
[06:39.30]a life in between.
